# vectorxform

- Label: Vector Transform
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 24 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/vectorxform.html
- Summary (EN): Applies a 3D transform to the values of an RGB layer, attribute or Vector VDB. Each value is treated as an XYZ position, transformed and written back. Output: transform.
- Résumé (FR) : Transforme en 3D les valeurs XYZ d'une couche RGB, d'un attribut ou d'un VDB vectoriel, sans déplacer les pixels.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the RGB layer, attribute or Vector VDB whose values define the XYZ positions", "mask (optional): per-pixel mask scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Mask: how much of the new value mixes with the original (default 1 uses only the new value); also selects which RGBA channels are affected", "Transform Order and Rotate Order", "Translate, Rotate (degrees), Scale (non-uniform), Shear, Uniform Scale", "Pivot Translate and Pivot Rotate: local pivot space", "Invert Transformation: applies the inverse transform"]

- Caveats: ["The node does not move pixels; each pixel is processed in place, so only its values change"]

